  "meta": {
    "name": "Dead-head maximum pressure 261030-1",
    "description": "Blocked-outlet (dead-head) maximum pressure vs frequency, pump 261030-1. The syringe controller holds the plunger still (motor energised, no regulation) and the pump pressurises the fixed volume: 60 s per step (ended early at 270 mbar, logged as stop_above = maximum >= 270), 5 s at 0 Hz, gentle release to ~3 mbar (15 mbar/s, never below), 15 s at 0 Hz. 2.5 V: 600, 800, 1000, 1300, 1600, 2000, 1300 Hz; 1 V: 600, 1300 Hz. Voltages by the RSD3305P, PPK2 on. ORDER: 1) config_prime_strong_261030-1.json with the outlet vented (check block >= ~200 uL/min at 600 Hz, else run it again); 2) connect the syringe through the stopcock, syringe EMPTY (room to pull back for the releases), stopcock closed to waste; 3) this config. Open the stopcock to waste before ANY manual syringe push: hand pushes against the closed line read 530-550 mbar on 2 Nov, beyond the sensor range.",
    "operator": "",
